    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this dispute is decided on the trip's GPS trace and fare breakdown, and the result is a partial refund of SGD 3.55 to the rider.\n\nWhat happened. The booked optimal route was 11.8 km / 15.9 min. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02854) measures the trip at 15.06 km, an excess of 3.26 km = 27.6% of optimal. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing figure and forbids using the rounded 15.1 km convenience copy on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02854), so the excess is 3.26 km, not 3.3 km. Both arms of the establishment gate are met (over 20% of optimal and over 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is established. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (it is neither over 50% of optimal nor over 8.0 km absolute), so POL-RD-06's uplift and its conduct referral do not run; and in any event no repeat pattern exists — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1/387 = 0.0026 (below 0.05 with 387 trips, well over the 40-trip minimum). The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags was mentioned only to say that POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting it for the trailing-window field, so it was correctly not used as a ground. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 119 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0 seconds. The deviation therefore stands on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nThe fare arithmetic (POL-RD-02). charged_total = 21.45 (EV-FARE-02854). recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 11.8 + 0.28 x 15.9) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee = 17.902, the surge multiplier of 1.0 being read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (it is not carried on the trip record). Refund = 21.45 - 17.902 = 3.548, rounded UP to SGD 3.55. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90%-of-charged full-refund share, so a partial refund issues. Because this is a rider-filed dispute, payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, PARTIAL_REFUND moves $3.55 back to the rider (POL-GEN-03); NO_ACTION would leave the charge in place. The monetary effect ($3.55) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 it executes automatically and the case does not queue for human release.\n\nThe driver's traffic explanation. The driver says there was a jam on the expressway and that traffic was diverting. No traffic advisory covers this trip window: EV-ADVIS-02854-01 is MISSING (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, no payload), so POL-RD-03's comparison — a named road the optimal route traverses, an overlapping validity window, a route that leaves and rejoins the corridor — cannot be run, and the assertion reduces no excess and supplies no amended optimal (POL-RD-08, POL-RD-13(2)). I am not escalating on it. The counterparty statement names no advisory evidence ID at all, and POL-RD-13(1) provides that where the asserting party names no evidence ID for an advisory, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5) — an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one. The driver's advocate's submission that the driver 'points to' the advisory artifact is not borne out by the record, which is why that escalation argument does not carry. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers all match (TRP-02854), the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree, and the refund is neither over SGD 150 nor above charged_total. Escalation is therefore not warranted and the money moves.\n\nNo exculpatory clause is available on the facts. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02854) is empty, so there is no rider instruction under POL-RD-04; no pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 has nothing to re-quote; vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. No driver compensation arises: the billed distance (15.1 km) is not less than the trace distance (15.06 km), so there is no POL-RD-04 shortfall to compensate. No billing-integrity referral arises either — the fare breakdown carries no ERP lines, no airport surcharge and no phantom gantry, so POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged, and the referrals list is empty. No artifact below weight 1.0 carries any deciding fact; EV-ADVIS-02854-01 is at weight 0.0 but carried no fact, only its own absence."
  },
